# A change to which sites a group holds fails the lint until `coupled --update`
# records it in the registry, so a change to the registry is a change to what's coupled. The
# branch ruleset requires a pull request with no approvals, but a code owner's review: a pull
# request touching only the files below waits for a person, and every other one merges once CI
# passes. Agents push under their own account, since no one can approve their own pull request.

# The registry, and the settings, whose exclude list and registry-file could take sites out of
# the lint without the registry changing.
# COUPLED:registry-path: owners
/.config/coupled-registry.toml @demo-org/coupling-reviewers
/.config/coupled.toml @demo-org/coupling-reviewers

# What enforces the review: CI, which runs the lint, and this file.
/.github/workflows/ @demo-org/coupling-reviewers
/.github/CODEOWNERS @demo-org/coupling-reviewers
